From acb285af0b4be10382533664d7c772645c018e8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 03:18:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02239/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE E1
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; NEW
 mechanism = cross-game transfer) -- does the ARC learned verifier
 (arc_value_learner: state->steps-to-go), trained on the SOLVED games' solve
 traces, reduce SEARCH STATES on a HELD-OUT game (leave-one-game-out)?
 research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone. .398
 (exp4306) PROVED online/retrieval adaptation HELPS (+0.529, powered) -- so
 re-measuring it is churn; the NEW frontier (per ops/verifier_registry.yaml:
 'cross-game verifier transfer: not yet pursued; POC is per-game value head')
 is whether a value-head trained on OTHER games transfers its
 search-efficiency benefit to a new game. This is the north-star EFFICIENCY
 axis (fewer search states = more efficient solve, the Exp1165
 ~4x-fewer-actions thesis) + the self-learning mandate in ONE. Train
 arc_value_learner on the reproducibly-solved games' traces
 (r11l/ls20/wa30/lp85); test LEAVE-ONE-GAME-OUT: does the transferred
 value-head reduce OfflineSolver search states on the held-out game vs an
 untrained/uniform heuristic? Report cross_game_state_reduction (held-out
 states_uniform / states_transferred) + per-held-out-game reads. Honest null
 (per-game heads do NOT transfer, reduction ~1.0) LOGS a 'game-invariant ARC
 value representation' missing-verifier gap. verifier_is_oracle=false. NO TRM
 training; NO live-LoRA; NO weight mutation of any LLM (the value-head is a
 tiny learned heuristic over solver state, CPU).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
